# How authentication works in these .http files
# 1. Run one of the login requests below and copy `accessToken` from the response.
# 2. Put it in a file named `.env` next to this repo's root (or your workspace root):
#        YOCABS_TOKEN=eyJhbGciOi...
#    Every other .http file sends it as `Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv YOCABS_TOKEN}}`.
# Access tokens live 30 minutes; use /auth/refresh with the refreshToken to get a new pair.
# Which token you need: tourist (search-to-booking), partner (fleet, pricing, drivers), admin (/admin/**).

### 1. Tourist / partner / driver: request a one-time code
# In development the code is printed in the API log:  [DEV OTP] code 123456 for ******3210
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/otp/request
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mobile": "9876543210"
}

### 2. Verify the code -> tokens (a new mobile number becomes a TOURIST account)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mobile": "9876543210",
  "code": "123456"
}

### 3. Travel partner self-registration (creates a partner awaiting approval + the owner login)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/partner/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "mobile": "9123456780",
  "ownerName": "Amit Kumar",
  "businessName": "Jaha Travels"
}

### 4. Admin login (email + password)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/admin/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "your-bootstrap-admin-password"
}

### 5. Refresh (rotates the refresh token; reusing an old one revokes the whole session)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN"
}

### 6. Who am I
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{$dotenv YOCABS_TOKEN}}

### 7. Logout
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN"
}
